  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Veterans Evaluation Services obligated $1.7B in FY2026 to date. Veterans Evaluation Services received 25 federal awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $66.5M. Obligations fell 18.2% year over year. Historical obligations show a multi-year rise into FY25 followed by a partial-year pullback: FY21 was $617M, FY22 was $691M, FY23 was $693M, FY24 was $1.1B, and FY25 was $2B. The FY26-to-date total of $1.7B is a partial fiscal-year number. These figures are contract obligations, except where tables list total contract values for largest awards or expiring contracts. Contractors and subcontractors evaluating opportunities with Veterans Evaluation Services should note the concentration implied by a high average award size and the recent year-over-year decline when assessing near-term market activity with this vendor.",
